# The QA verify's -Dit.test, one class per line. THE LIST IS NOT DERIVED: a class this file stops
# naming is written and never runs, silently, and there is no wildcard to fall back on — `*IT` would
# pull PackagedSurfaceIT back in, which does real git pushes through a CGI fixture and a
# pseudo-terminal and is why skipITs is true in the root pom to begin with.
#
# The five story classes come first and in this order, which is the order failsafe runs them in
# anyway (it orders by FQCN within a @TestProfile group) and is load-bearing: they share one profile,
# TokenValidationBootstrapIT.PackagedWithMockIdp, so the group is one launched process and one
# embedded postgres, and the bootstrap IT owns the run's first bearer and the JWKS fetch after it.
# See AGENTS.md § Userflows.

TokenValidationBootstrapIT
ProjectCatalogueIT
EpicPlanningIT
AccessRefusalIT
CatalogueReviewIT

# The two pin tests, which are not stories and not in that profile group at all: plain JUnit, no
# @TestProfile, no Quarkus application, no bearer, so their position here decides nothing. They are
# the gates that make this repository's two image pins mean something — qits/workspace, which a
# refinement container starts (WorkspaceImage.VERSION off the pinned qits-workspace-daemon-protocol),
# and qits/project-agent, which a project's agent container starts (ProjectAgentImage.VERSION off the
# pinned qits-projects-daemon-protocol). Each downloads the daemon at exactly the pinned version,
# runs it as a process against a stand-in host and round-trips the real protocol, so a daemon bump
# that breaks the wire fails THIS fold rather than the next live refinement or agent container. Drop
# either line and its pin is an untested number again. Both need the artifacts origin, which they
# derive by cutting qits.maven.repository.url at /artifacts/ — the archetype's verify exports and
# passes it; with no origin at all they skip, which is the one state a CI step is never in.

RefinementDaemonPinIT
ProjectAgentDaemonPinIT
